From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 06:30:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] drm/msm/dsi: 12nm: program the PLL in prepare

The rate and divider ops wrote PLL registers piecemeal and clobbered
each other (set_rate reset the GP divider select), and recalc_rate
always returned the cached rate, so the tree kept the bootloader's
3.072 GHz. Record the requested rate and divider selections and
commit them together before the lock sequence, as downstream does.
Also fix the /2 post-divider decode, the swapped registers in
restore_state, and leave SSC off as downstream does by default.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
